# Noirix device identity reporting module.

config NOIRIX_AUTH
    bool "Noirix device identity reporting (device-id whitelist)"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO_RPC
    select HWINFO
    help
      Registers the "noirix__auth" ZMK Studio RPC subsystem, which reports the
      MCU unique ID (device_id) so the host (dya-studio) can check it against a
      whitelist of authorized device IDs. No shared secret or MAC is involved;
      the host stores whitelisted device IDs as SHA-256 hashes.

      Depends on CONFIG_ZMK_STUDIO_RPC (the custom RPC subsystem is registered
      via ZMK Studio's custom subsystem API). On a split keyboard only the
      central half enables ZMK_STUDIO_RPC, so this is only built there.
